   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "t:ftm",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "If $\\nu$ has a continuous cdf $F$, the regret of \\fem{} satisfies, for all time horizons $T\\in \\N$, \\[ R_T \\le \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\brb{ 1 + \\ln (T-1) } \\;. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Regret is sup_p E[sum G_t(p) - G_t(P_t)], i.e. through expected rewards (pseudo-regret). FEM does not use T. Proof assumes T>=2."
  },
  {
   "id": "r2",
